<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21112] LBUG in osc_req_attr_set() on buffered IO with nolock mount</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21112</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;A client mounted with "-o nolock" hits an LBUG when doing buffered&lt;br/&gt;
(non-O_DIRECT) IO. The dirty pages are cached without any DLM lock, and&lt;br/&gt;
the crash happens at writeback when osc_req_attr_set() looks for a lock&lt;br/&gt;
covering the page:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;LustreError: (osc_object.c:385:osc_req_attr_set()) uncovered page!
LustreError: (osc_object.c:394:osc_req_attr_set()) No lock resource
LustreError: (osc_object.c:398:osc_req_attr_set()) LBUG
Workqueue: events brw_queue_work [osc]
Call trace:
 lbug_with_loc+0x50/0xa0 [libcfs]
 osc_req_attr_set+0x47c/0x550 [osc]
 cl_req_attr_set+0xc4/0x1b8 [obdclass]
 osc_build_rpc+0x54c/0x1580 [osc]
 osc_check_rpcs+0x7c8/0x1440 [osc]
 __osc_io_unplug+0xb8/0xf8 [osc]
 brw_queue_work+0x70/0x158 [osc]&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducer:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;mount -t lustre -o nolock &amp;lt;mgsnid&amp;gt;:/&amp;lt;fsname&amp;gt; /mnt/lustre
dd if=/dev/urandom of=/mnt/lustre/f bs=1M count=4
sync&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
